Findings documented (not assumed)
8 microservices on ports 8080–8088 (8084 unused), 7 PostgreSQL databases
38 REST endpoints from actual controllers (corrects outdated Backend/API.md)
No tests, Docker, or CI/CD in the repo
Security gap: all services use permitAll(); only auth-service parses JWT
Register page uses localStorage only — backend POST /auth/register is not called
Doctor approve/reject is UI-only; no status update endpoint
Admin /hospitals uses static mock data; super-admin hospitals use the API
Demo credentials in seed SQL (admin1@, doctor1@, patient1@) differ from older README examples
Questions that need your input
License — no LICENSE file in the repo
Production URLs and deployment topology
CI/CD — how builds/deploys are automated
Monitoring/logging in production
Intended registration flow — backend API vs localStorage page
Authoritative demo credentials — seed SQL vs README
Whether /auth/refresh and /auth/me are planned (documented but not implemented)
HIPAA/compliance requirements for medical data
Project ownership and contribution process
Multi-tenancy — is per-hospital admin isolation required?
If you want changes, say which sections to expand (e.g. OpenAPI export, runbooks, or architecture decision records).